{"title":"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a triangle with integer side lengths, one side is three times as long as a second side, and the length of the third side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the greatest possible perimeter of the triangle? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/5317dd78c511572b63872c86fdf07ad8074e16a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 43\\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 44\\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 45\\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 46\\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the length of the first side. \n</p><p>The lengths of the sides are: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality\" title=\"Triangle Inequality\">Triangle Inequality</a>,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/03120039a08083a222d4e08b7cbeaf9700cc8a4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x &lt; x + 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11a57d480de79ad5258de93fb515f75e0aaedc49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x &lt; 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a29258df76764bf01953b43e2fe1005312853d9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; \\frac{15}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The greatest integer satisfying this inequality is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>So the greatest possible perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/4467744b95bcf9cb55e3bac9969dea05376dbf15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 + 3\\cdot7 + 15 =\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"194\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B\">2006 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</